 "known_defects_found_by_this_run": [
  "pit_replay.run_pilot() updates the pit_replay_run row only on the success path. The abort left run_id 1 at status='running', finished_at=NULL, n_entities=NULL, n_dates=4 while it in fact covers 2 dates and 15234 entity-dates. The row was deliberately NOT corrected here: correcting it means opening a writer at 4.132 GiB free. Move that UPDATE into a finally block.",
  "pit_replay.run_pilot() builds its report dict locally, so an exception inside the date loop discards every per-date stats dict (refusal tallies, signature tallies, block tallies). Those were reconstructed from the pilot database instead. Accumulate the report outside the try, or write each date's stats as it completes.",
  "pit_replay_meter.Meter double-counts rows: both mark(rows=...) and table_scope increment _rows_written, so meter.report()['work']['rows_written_by_table'] reads 396084/121872/11164 against a true 198042/60936/5582. The byte measurements are unaffected.",
  "The engine assembles an entire cross-section into Python lists before its first insert. On a 7.45 GiB-RAM machine this is what actually consumed the disk, via pagefile expansion, not the WAL. Streaming the inserts in chunks would remove the largest transient this pilot measured."
 ]
